{"id": "EUVD-2026-103083", "enisaUuid": "542f54c3-286d-367a-a870-08a611356ff7", "description": "waynboot-mall through 2.0.0 contains a missing authentication vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to send arbitrary email by calling the anonymously mapped /callback/email endpoint. Attackers can POST caller-supplied subject, content, and recipient to EmailController.sendEmail, sending messages from the operator's SMTP account for phishing, spam, and mail quota exhaustion.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:18:14", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/waynboot-mall-unauth-callback-order-forgery-cancel-mail-relay", "https://github.com/wayn111/waynboot-mall/blob/v2.0.0/waynboot-mobile-api/src/main/java/com/wayn/mobile/api/controller/callback/EmailController.java#L32-L42", "https://github.com/wayn111/waynboot-mall/blob/v2.0.0/waynboot-mobile-api/src/main/java/com/wayn/mobile/framework/config/SecurityConfig.java#L66", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/waynboot-mall-through-2.0.0-missing-authentication-via-callback-email-mail-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111661", "GHSA-xgfp-xxg8-vfxp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d380d012-c5df-35b9-8726-05cc3d901ff3", "product": {"name": "waynboot-mall", "vendor": {"name": "wayn111"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e36e569-801e-3017-9c65-6bc9ec08450d", "vendor": {"name": "wayn111"}}], "isExploited": false}